Kubernetes Init Container Deployment (ic-deploy-devops)
Project Overview
This project demonstrates the implementation of Kubernetes Init Containers to handle configuration pre-requisites prior to starting the main application container. In this scenario, an init container provisions a required configuration file on a shared volume, which is subsequently read by the main container.

Architecture & Components
Deployment Name: ic-deploy-devops

Replicas: 1

Labels: app: ic-devops (applied to both Deployment selector and Pod template metadata)

Storage (Volume): ic-volume-devops configured as an emptyDir type for temporary pod-lifetime shared storage.

Init Container (ic-msg-devops):

Image: fedora:latest

Command: ["/bin/bash", "-c", "echo Init Done - Welcome to xFusionCorp Industries > /ic/beta"]

Volume Mount: Mounted at /ic (ic-volume-devops)

Main Container (ic-main-devops):

Image: fedora:latest

Command: ["/bin/bash", "-c", "while true; do cat /ic/beta; sleep 5; done"]

Volume Mount: Mounted at /ic (ic-volume-devops)

Deployment Manifest (deployment.yaml)
YAML
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: ic-deploy-devops
  labels:
    app: ic-devops
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: ic-devops
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: ic-devops
    spec:
      initContainers:
        - name: ic-msg-devops
          image: fedora:latest
          command: ["/bin/bash", "-c", "echo Init Done - Welcome to xFusionCorp Industries > /ic/beta"]
          volumeMounts:
            - name: ic-volume-devops
              mountPath: /ic
      containers:
        - name: ic-main-devops
          image: fedora:latest
          command: ["/bin/bash", "-c", "while true; do cat /ic/beta; sleep 5; done"]
          volumeMounts:
            - name: ic-volume-devops
              mountPath: /ic
      volumes:
        - name: ic-volume-devops
          emptyDir: {}
Quick Start & Verification
Apply the Manifest:

Bash
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
Check Pod Initialization and Status:

Bash
kubectl get pods
Verify Init Container Execution Logs:

Bash
kubectl logs deployment/ic-deploy-devops -c ic-msg-devops
Verify Main Container Output:

Bash
kubectl logs deployment/ic-deploy-devops -c ic-main-devops
Technical Review & Summary
Execution Status: Successful

Validation Results:

The init container (ic-msg-devops) successfully initialized, mounted the emptyDir volume, and wrote the expected greeting string into /ic/beta before exiting cleanly with status code 0.

The main container (ic-main-devops) successfully initialized after the init container completed, continuously reading and streaming the expected configuration message (Init Done - Welcome to xFusionCorp Industries) from the shared volume mount.

Key Takeaway: The init container pattern successfully decouples pre-deployment configuration steps from application container images, providing a clean separation of concerns for Kubernetes workloads.
